# A recursion entered by a tail call from a function outside it, the shape of
# a one-line library wrapper, names its cycle when it runs out of stack. The
# call is made as an ordinary one, so the record can be put back when the
# recursion returns (kanso#1991). The float keeps the accumulator rewrite
# from turning the recursion into a loop.
fn depth 0
  0.0

fn depth k
  0.5 + depth (k - 1)

fn deep_from n
  depth n

pub play = print "{deep_from 100000000}"
